# NGCheck Backend Development Rules

## C# Coding Standards

### General C# Rules
- Use C# 11+ features where appropriate
- Prefer var for local variables when type is obvious
- Use expression-bodied members for simple methods
- Use null-conditional operators (?. and ??)
- Implement IDisposable with using statements
- Use readonly for fields that shouldn't change
- Prefer string interpolation over concatenation

### ASP.NET Core Specific
```csharp
// Controller structure example
[ApiController]
[Route("api/[controller]")]
[Authorize]
public class ExampleController : ControllerBase
{
    private readonly IExampleService _exampleService;
    private readonly ILogger<ExampleController> _logger;
    
    public ExampleController(IExampleService exampleService, ILogger<ExampleController> logger)
    {
        _exampleService = exampleService;
        _logger = logger;
    }
    
    [HttpGet("{id}")]
    [ProducesResponseType(typeof(ExampleDto), 200)]
    [ProducesResponseType(404)]
    public async Task<IActionResult> GetById(int id)
    {
        try
        {
            var result = await _exampleService.GetByIdAsync(id);
            return result != null ? Ok(result) : NotFound();
        }
        catch (Exception ex)
        {
            _logger.LogError(ex, "Error getting example by id: {Id}", id);
            return StatusCode(500, "An error occurred");
        }
    }
}
```

