### Entity Framework Core
- Use fluent API for configuration
- Implement audit fields (CreatedAt, UpdatedAt, CreatedBy, UpdatedBy)
- Use value converters for enums
- Configure relationships explicitly
- Use Include() judiciously to avoid N+1 queries
- Implement specifications pattern for complex queries

### DTOs and Mapping
- Create separate DTOs for Create, Update, and Response
- Use AutoMapper for entity-DTO conversions
- Validate DTOs with FluentValidation
- Never expose navigation properties in DTOs

### Dependency Injection
```csharp
// In Program.cs or Startup.cs
builder.Services.AddScoped<IExampleService, ExampleService>();
builder.Services.AddScoped<IExampleRepository, ExampleRepository>();
builder.Services.AddAutoMapper(typeof(MappingProfile));
```

### Middleware and Filters
- Implement global exception handling middleware
- Use action filters for cross-cutting concerns
- Implement request/response logging middleware
- Add correlation ID middleware for request tracking

### API Versioning
- Use URL versioning: /api/v1/[controller]
- Maintain backward compatibility
- Document breaking changes
- Use API versioning package

### Background Services
- Use IHostedService for background tasks
- Implement proper cancellation token handling
- Use Hangfire for scheduled jobs
- Log all background operations

